From: Caboose <caboose@local>
Subject: [PATCH 99/99] Give a call whose reply was lost the outputs of a call made after the loss

A call made once the executor is gone returns at entry with stand-in outputs: unique local
handles for every object it creates or allocates (arrays included), layout support, sizes and
counts a lost device allows. A call already under way when the executor went read its reply
from the ended stream instead, which reads as the loss result in every word: with
CABOOSE_GPU_ON_LOSS=quiet that is zeros, a null handle or an "unsupported" layout. Zink in the
compositor then crashed on a null descriptor set layout (zink_descriptor_program_init).

Each call that has stand-in outputs now notes the thread's lost replies at entry
(caboose::completion::lostReplies, counted by the socket transport's lost reply) and, if one
was lost during the call, gives the same stand-in outputs and result as a call made after
the loss. Calls whose stand-in would repeat a side effect the call already had (frees,
resets, binds, maps) are left as they were. An instance or device asked for while the
executor is gone fails to initialize instead of returning a handle that was never written.
---
diff --git a/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/autogenerated/VkEncoder.cpp b/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/autogenerated/VkEncoder.cpp
index b330dd3..60de1b5 100644
--- a/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/autogenerated/VkEncoder.cpp
+++ b/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/autogenerated/VkEncoder.cpp
@@ -1013,7 +1013,8 @@ VkResult VkEncoder::vkCreateInstance(const VkInstanceCreateInfo* pCreateInfo,
                                      uint32_t doLock) {
     (void)doLock;
     // The executor is gone: report device loss, and never read garbage replies into outputs.
-    if (caboose::completion::lostCall()) return VkResult(caboose::completion::lostResult());
+    if (caboose::completion::lostCall()) return VK_ERROR_INITIALIZATION_FAILED;
+    const uint64_t cabooseLostReplies = caboose::completion::lostReplies;
     bool queueSubmitWithCommandsEnabled =
         sFeatureBits & VULKAN_STREAM_FEATURE_QUEUE_SUBMIT_WITH_COMMANDS_BIT;
     if (!queueSubmitWithCommandsEnabled && doLock) this->lock();
@@ -1121,6 +1122,8 @@ VkResult VkEncoder::vkCreateInstance(const VkInstanceCreateInfo* pCreateInfo,
         stream->clearPool();
     }
     if (!queueSubmitWithCommandsEnabled && doLock) this->unlock();
+    // A reply lost during the call: the outputs a call made after the loss gets.
+    if (caboose::completion::lostReplies != cabooseLostReplies) return VK_ERROR_INITIALIZATION_FAILED;
     return caboose::completion::heldLoss(vkCreateInstance_VkResult_return);
 }
 
